   "parameter_provenance": {
    "eos.V0": "Abstract and Table 2, preferred FPMD-LDA Vinet column; 46.17 A^3 per formula unit at 1000 K and zero pressure.",
    "eos.K0": "Abstract gives K_T0 at 1000 K as 203.95 GPa; this value independently reproduces the one-decimal Table 1 isochors. The PDF text extraction of Table 2 reads 203.5 GPa and is preserved as a source inconsistency.",
    "eos.K0_prime": "Table 2, preferred FPMD-LDA Vinet column; 4.76.",
    "thermal.Tr": "Section 4 and Table 2; 1000 K reference isotherm because the cubic phase is unstable at 300 K.",
    "thermal.theta0": "Table 2; 1100 K, fixed.",
    "thermal.gamma0": "Abstract and Table 2; 1.576.",
    "thermal.q": "Abstract and Table 2; 0.96.",
    "thermal.n": "Tange et al. (2009), equation 5, defines n as atoms per formula unit; CaSiO3 has five atoms."
   },
   "validity": {
    "pressure_gpa": [
     0.0,
     150.0
    ],
    "temperature_k": [
     1000.0,
     4000.0
    ],
    "volume_ratio": [
     0.7,
     1.0
    ],
    "notes": [
     "The stated FPMD sampling spans approximately 0-150 GPa; Table 1 publishes fitted isochors from 1000 to 4000 K and V/V0=0.70-1.00.",
     "Section 2 prints a computational temperature range of 300-1500 K, but Figure 2 explicitly labels calculated FPMD points at 1000, 2000, 3000, and 4000 K. Because the raw state table is unavailable, that source inconsistency cannot be resolved; the executable temperature range is conservatively tied to the unambiguous plotted and tabulated 1000-4000 K EOS output.",
     "The paper warns that the very-low-pressure, high-temperature corner lies outside cubic CaSiO3 stability or near melting, so this rectangular numerical envelope is not a phase-stability guarantee."
    ]
   },
   "notes": "Preferred Vinet reference isotherm plus a constant-q Mie-Gruneisen-Debye thermal pressure relative to 1000 K. The integrated Debye-temperature law follows equations 4-10 of Tange et al. (2009), which Kawai and Tsuchiya explicitly adopt; n=5 for one CaSiO3 formula unit. V0 is already one cubic Pm-3m conventional cell because Z=1. The input stresses came from LDA-PWSCF NVT FPMD on an 80-atom 2x2x1 tetragonal-supercell representation constrained to cubic metrics, with 50 Ry cutoff, a 2x2x2 k-point grid, 1 fs steps, 1 ps equilibration, and 5 ps production averages. Figure 1 reports a convergence benchmark near 15 GPa and 2000 K: the 2x2x2 sampling gives diagonal stresses 15.3, 15.5, and 15.2 GPa, compared with 16.0, 16.1, and 14.6 GPa at Gamma only; no volume is printed, so this is not an EOS-fit row. No parameter uncertainties or covariance are reported, so missing errors are null rather than zero. The alternate BM3 column is intentionally not added because this contribution is limited to one literature EOS record and the article plots and abstracts the Vinet result. The abstract's K0=203.95 GPa reproduces Table 1 (for example 184.42 GPa rounds to 184.5 GPa at V/V0=0.70 and 4000 K), whereas the PDF-extracted Table 2 value 203.5 GPa predicts 184.06 GPa; the benchmark-consistent abstract value is retained. Section 2's printed 300-1500 K simulation range conflicts with calculated 1000-4000 K points in Figure 2 and cannot be resolved without the raw state table.",
   "identifier": "ca_perovskite_kawai_2014_vinet_mgd_3",
   "fit_datasets": [],
